-- title:
--   Supersingular closed point on the j-chart, diamond frame, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell_g$ be a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, write $\kappa$ for its residue field, and let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,M'$ over $\kappa$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places in the sense of `ssPlaces q M' κ` (rational places which are affine geometric and whose value on `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q κ`, the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic Weierstrass models over $\kappa$ have trivial $q$-torsion). Assume `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le$ `fieldBar q M'`, that is, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field lies inside the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the function field of level $q^2M'$ with level group `levelH q M'`, the units of $\mathbb Z/q^2M'$ congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (a valuation subring of integers, a surjective residue homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and its residue map, together with a degree-preserving map on places), and assume it is computed coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element is $R_0$-integral and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Fix $s \in W$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element lying in $A$, and put $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$); assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, that $A_0$ is henselian, that its residue field is algebraically closed, and that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of `levelH q M'` with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ both modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell_g$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq k_0((q))$ obtained as the $k_0$-base change `laurentBaseChange` of `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁`, equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure forming a scalar tower with $k_0$. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq`, with $j \neq 0$, assume this image lies in $K$ and that the resulting element lies in $C :=$ `chartAlgFin` $A_0\,K\,j$, the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A_0[j]$. Then there is a maximal ideal $y$ of $C$ such that: the image of $\pi_0$ in $C$ lies in $y$; for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`; and for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is $R_0$-integral, which is regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which `jq` is regular (non-negative order), and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for which the coefficientwise image of $g$ lies in $K$ and gives an element of $C$, and for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals the value of the $R_0$-residue of $g$ at $s$, the difference in $C$ of the element given by $g$ and the image of $c$ lies in $y$.
--
--   This is the $q=3$, $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-diamond variant of the construction of a supersingular closed point on the $j$-finite chart of the integral model at level $H_1$ over the small field of constants $k_0$, lying over a prescribed supersingular place $s$ of the level-$M'$ function field in characteristic $q$, and at which the specified level-$M'$ functions reduce to their values at $s$. It feeds the later construction of invariants avoiding prescribed valuation subrings and the assembly of the supersingular discrete valuation ring with its affine chart, poles, nodes and inertia data at level $q^2M'$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_Diamond_exists_isMaximal_chartAlgFin_mem_ssJSet_over_of_ssPlaces_of_eq_three_of_dvd.lean

